---
title: Brownies
author: Deliah Smith
servings: 48
cook time: 25 minutes
---

Preheat the oven to 180°C/gas mark 4. Line your brownie pan - I think it's worth lining the sides as well as the base - with foil, parchment or Bake-O-Glide.

Melt @butter{375%g}(soft unsalted) and @dark chocolate{375%g} together in a large heavy-based #pan{}.

In a bowl or large wide-mouthed measuring jug, beat @large eggs{6} with @caster sugar{500%g} and @vanilla extract{1%tbsp}.

Measure @plain flour{225%g} into another bowl and add @salt{1%tsp}.

When the chocolate mixture has melted, let it cool a bit before beating in the eggs and then the @walnuts{300%g}(chopped) and flour. Beat to combine smoothly and then scrape out of the saucepan into the lined pan.

Bake for about ~{25%minutes}. When it's ready, the top should be dried to a paler brown speckle, but the middle still dark and dense and gooey.

> Even with such a big batch you do need to keep alert, keep checking: the difference between gungy brownies and dry brownies is only a few minutes; remember that they will continue to cook as they cool.
